{"id":"claim:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--an-temporal-noun-arrival","revision":1,"topic":"topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topics":["topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--grammaticalized-uses"],"statement":{"en":"The existential verb an can express the arrival of a time period or change to existence when used with temporal nouns.","ja":"存在動詞 an は時を表す名詞と共に用いられると、その時が到来すること（存在への変化）を表すことができる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":["with temporal nouns"]},"forms":["an","paykar an"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0116-05","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0051-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--an-is-the-singular-existential-verb-meaning-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topics":["topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--number-suppletion"],"statement":{"en":"'an is the singular existential verb meaning \"to exist / to be\".","ja":"'an は単数主語をとる存在動詞（「ある」「いる」）である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["'an"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0069-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--okay-is-the-plural-existential-verb-meaning-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topics":["topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--number-suppletion"],"statement":{"en":"'okay is the plural existential verb meaning \"to exist / to be\".","ja":"'okay は複数主語をとる存在動詞（「ある」「いる」）である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["'okay"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0069-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--in-the-saru-and-chitose-dialects-the-plural","revision":1,"topic":"topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topics":["topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--number-suppletion"],"statement":{"en":"In the Saru and Chitose dialects, the plural form of the existence verb okay appears without final -y as oka.","ja":"沙流および千歳方言では、存在動詞の複数形 okay は末尾の -y が脱落した形 oka として現れる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["okáy","oká"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawafukazawa2022@handbook-epub/l0050-14","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--the-equative-construction-equivalent-can-take-an-exist","revision":1,"topic":"topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topics":["topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The equative construction equivalent can take an 'exist' (the antonym of isam 'not exist') as its predicate.","ja":"同等比較構文相当表現は、isam「存在しない」の反意語であるan「存在する」を述語として取ることができる。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["an","isam"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2015@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0012-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--the-same-verbs-of-existence-and-non-existence","revision":1,"topic":"topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topics":["topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The same verbs of existence and non-existence ('an [SG], 'okay [PL], 'isam) are used whether the existing entity is human or non-human.","ja":"存在・非存在を表す動詞（'an〔単〕、'okay〔複〕、'isam）は、存在の主体が人間でもモノでも同じ動詞を使う。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["'an","'okay","'isam"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0025-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--the-existential-verb-an-and-the-copula-ne","revision":1,"topic":"topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topics":["topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The existential verb an and the copula ne can both express a static state and a change of state.","ja":"存在動詞anおよびコピュラneは、静的な状態と状態変化の双方を表すことができる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["an","ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0091-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--locative-be-exist-is-expressed-by-the-intransitive","revision":1,"topic":"topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topics":["topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--valency-frame"],"statement":{"en":"Locative 'be/exist' is expressed by the intransitive locative copula an/oka 'exist, appear (SG/PL)'.","ja":"存在・所在の「ある／いる」は、自動詞である特殊な所在係辞 an/oka「存在する、現れる（単数／複数）」によって表される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["an","oka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0022-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--there-are-three-ways-to-express-the-location","revision":1,"topic":"topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topics":["topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka","topic:clause/existential-locational-an-oka--valency-frame"],"statement":{"en":"There are three ways to express the location of existence: using adverbs such as teeta 'here', taata 'there', and nahta 'where'; attaching the postposition 'ohta to place names; or attaching the locative suffix -ta to positional nouns.","ja":"存在の場所を表すには、teeta、taata、nahta などの副詞を使う方法、場所名詞に後置詞 'ohta をつける方法、位置名詞に場所格語尾 -ta をつけて用いる方法の3つがある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["teeta","taata","nahta","'ohta","-ta"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0025-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
